input.command:
node --check game.js && node --input-type=module <<'EOF'
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const css = readFileSync('styles.css','utf8');
let depth=0, line=1, bad=null;
for (const ch of css){ if(ch==='\n') line++; if(ch==='{') depth++; if(ch==='}'){depth--; if(depth<0&&!bad) bad=line;} }
console.log('css brace depth', depth, 'bad', bad);
const html = readFileSync('index.html','utf8');
const ids=[...html.matchAll(/id="([^"]+)"/g)].map(m=>m[1]);
console.log('duplicate ids', ids.filter((id,i)=>ids.indexOf(id)!==i));
const js=readFileSync('game.js','utf8');
const refs=[...js.matchAll(/\$\('#([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)'/g)].map(m=>m[1]);
console.log('missing refs', [...new Set(refs)].filter(id=>!ids.includes(id)));
EOF

content.text:
Now create validation script. Note `playwright` chromium executable path /usr/bin/chromium. The server 3002 is running.

Let me write the script with assertions and screenshots. Keep in mind animations/transitions require waits for computed styles. Use waitForTimeout after selection.

Also test annex against Argentina etc. After restarting campaigns, state resets.

For the military rail toast: click foreign US, then click military rail; relation actions visible; the heading scrolled into view. Check that no toast appears? Since `selectCountry` doesn't toast; previous toast may persist from earlier actions. We can hide by waiting 2700ms or check relation actions. Not critical.

Check `.country.player-country.selected` computed fill equals rgb(138,169,133).

Check small viewport overflow: document.documentElement.scrollWidth and body.scrollWidth; body overflow hidden so scrollWidth may still exceed. Use `Math.max(doc.scrollWidth, body.scrollWidth) <= width + 1`.

Check start modal bounding box within viewport and modal scrollHeight >= clientHeight.

At 480x320, start modal max-height 216 (320-104). Country cards 10 items 2 rows of 36 + gaps + header (h2 19*2 lines ~40 + p + labels + foot) likely >216 → scrollable. Test scrollHeight > clientHeight allowed, and modal fits viewport.

Selecting Brazil via card requires scrolling within modal? Playwright locator click auto-scrolls into view. Fine.

After start at 480x320, shell height 320. Map stage width? theater: 36 + 150+? +188 = 374 min; viewport 480 → map 256. Check map width >= 200.

Footer timeline: 118 + 1fr + 168 = 286; fits 480. Time controls 3 buttons: pause 34? compact sets height 27, widths default pause 34, speed 42, advance padding 8 + text; total ~34+42+90+gaps=174 > 168 → may overflow slightly. `.time-controls` justify-content flex-end; grid column 168; children may overflow left into timeline center? Could overlap. At 480, 168 column for controls: pause 34 + speed 42 + advance (font 8, "AVANÇAR" ~40 + span 8 + padding 16 = ~64) + gaps 8 = 148. Fits 168. Good. At 400: same 168. Fine.

Top command bar at 480: insignia 28 + title (HEMISFÉRIO 14px ~85) + campaign-name (~100) + top stats (treasury/gdp/pop each min 0 ~60) + settings 23 + gaps ~8*5=40 + padding 16 → 28+85+100+180+23+40+16=472, fits barely. At 400: overflow likely. But top stats may shrink? `.top-stat{min-width:auto}` compact, but content doesn't wrap; top-stats margin-left auto, command-bar flex no wrap. Could overflow horizontally and be clipped. At 400x300 landscape, header content ~472 > 400 → cut off (probably settings button off-screen). That's a bug for very small landscape. Could hide campaign-name and some top stats at max-width 560. Let's add in small query:
```
.campaign-name{display:none}
.top-stats{gap:7px}
.top-stat:nth-child(2){display:none} /* PIB? */
```
But keeping key stats treasury/gdp/pop is nice. At 480, header fits ~472; at 400 need ~370. Hiding campaign-name (~100) gets 372, fits. Also game-title small maybe hide. Add `.campaign-name{display:none}` and `.game-title small{display:none}`. At 400: 28+85+180+23+40+16=372 fits. Good. At 480, comfortable.

But the top stats three items each ~60 = 180; treasury "$220 bi" width ~55, gdp "$2.31 tri" ~60, pop "216 mi" ~45 + icons 14 + gaps 4 + stat gap 8 → each ~80 → 240. Hmm. Could hide PIB at max-width 440. Let's add:
```
@media(orientation:landscape) and (max-width:440px) and (max-height:480px){.top-stat:nth-child(2){display:none}}
```
Then header ~28+85+160+23+40+16=352 fits 400. Good.

Also `.map-legend` at 400 width: four items ~ (SEU PAÍS 45 + PAÍSES 35 + CONFLITO 45 + ANEXADO 42) + gaps 18 + padding 12 = 197, fits map 176? Map width at 400: 400-36-188=176. Legend width 197 > map, overflows clipped. Could hide the legend on tiny screens or wrap. Set `.map-legend{flex-wrap:wrap;max-width:calc(100% - 14px);gap:5px 8px;font-size:5px}` at small query. Or hide legend at max-width 440. Simpler: `.map-legend{display:none}` at max-width 440. The legend isn't essential. Also map controls at 400 map width 176: controls width 26*3+32+18? ~128, fits. map location + controls in overlay with justify-between; map location text "TEATRO DAS AMÉRICAS" ~100 + controls 128 = 228 > 176 → overlap. Could hide `.map-location small` and maybe shorten. At small query hide `.map-location`? The overlay location is decorative. Hide `.map-location` at max-width 440, keep controls. Then controls align right. Good.

At 480 map width 256: location 100 + controls 128 = 228 fits. Fine. At 440 map width 216: 228 > 216 → slight overlap. Add max-width 460 hide location small? Let's set at max-width 480: `.map-location small{display:none}` reduces height not width. Hide `.map-location b`? Better hide whole `.map-location` at max-width 460. Add a second tiny query.

Do we need to support 400px landscape? The user says mobile responsive. Most phones landscape width >= 568 (iPhone SE 568, Android 640+). 480x320 is old. 400x300 is rare. We can add these safe rules anyway.

Also start modal at 400: width 342, country cards 5 columns each ~63 with padding 8, emoji 14 + text 8px "Estados Unidos" ~55 → card content 14+4+55+8 padding = 81 > 63 → text may wrap/overflow. `.country-card` display flex, b may wrap to two lines. min-height 36; wrapping increases height; okay. Could reduce to 2 columns at tiny sizes? Then 5 rows, modal scrolls a lot. 5 columns is okay with wrapping. Alternatively hide emoji at max-width 440 to give text room. Add `.country-card .emoji{display:none}` at max-width 440. Then card width 63, text 55 fits. Good.

Let's add these tiny rules after the small query, before portrait:
```
@media(orientation:landscape) and (max-width:460px) and (max-height:480px){
 .campaign-name{display:none}
 .game-title small{display:none}
 .map-location{display:none}
 .map-legend{display:none}
 .top-stats{gap:7px}
}
@media(orientation:landscape) and (max-width:420px) and (max-height:480px){
 .top-stat:nth-child(2){display:none}
 .country-card .emoji{display:none}
}
```
At 400 header: 28+85+ (treasury+pop ~140) +23 + gaps 32 + padding 16 = 324. Fits.

Now, at 480x320, header with campaign-name hidden and location visible: 28+85+ (3 stats ~200) +23+40+16=392 fits. Good.

Let's apply.

