content.text:
At 568x320, after selecting AR, relation buttons not fully visible in the actions panel. The scrollToDiplomacy aligns heading at panel top, but the panel height is small (~? theater 220, banner 62, tabs 30 → actions panel ~128). The relation buttons grid 2x2 min-height 38 + gap → 82 plus heading 21 + copy 2 lines ~30 → >128. Scrolling heading to top means buttons may extend beyond. The panel can scroll further, but auto-scroll only aligns heading. We need to scroll to show the relation buttons (maybe align buttons bottom or scroll heading enough). For small panels, better scroll so relationActions is visible, even if heading is partially above. Implement scrollToDiplomacy to prefer showing the relation actions: if buttons taller than panel, align their top; else align heading.

Compute:
```
const actions = $('#relationActions');
const panelRect...
const actionsRect...
const headingRect...
if (actionsRect.height <= panelRect.height - 8) {
  // ensure actions fully visible
  const targetTop = actionsRect.top - panelRect.top;
  if (targetTop + actionsRect.height > panelRect.height) panel.scrollTop += targetTop + actionsRect.height - panelRect.height + 6;
  else if (headingRect.top < panelRect.top) ...?
}
```
Simpler: scroll so that the relation actions block is fully visible, with heading above if possible:
```
const padding=6;
let delta = 0;
const headingTop = headingRect.top - panelRect.top;
const actionsBottom = actionsRect.bottom - panelRect.top;
if (actionsBottom > panelRect.height - padding) delta = actionsBottom - panelRect.height + padding;
else if (headingTop < padding) delta = headingTop - padding;
panel.scrollTop += delta;
```
But if actions bottom exceeds and heading top also below 0? The panel scrollTop adjusts by delta; if actions block itself taller than panel, aligning bottom hides heading/top of buttons. In 568x320, actions grid 2x2: each min-height 38 + gap 6 = 82. Panel height maybe 128; padding 6 → 116 available; 82 fits. Heading + copy may be scrolled above; that's okay, buttons visible. But the user might not see the heading; still okay. Ideally show heading plus at least first row; but full buttons more important.

Let me implement: scroll actions fully into view if possible; if actions taller than panel, align top.

```
function scrollToDiplomacy() {
  const panel=$('#actionsPanel'), heading=$('#diplomacyHeading'), actions=$('#relationActions');
  if (!panel||!heading||panel.classList.contains('hidden')) return;
  const panelRect=panel.getBoundingClientRect();
  const headingRect=heading.getBoundingClientRect();
  const pad=6;
  let delta = headingRect.top - panelRect.top - pad;
  if (actions && !actions.classList.contains('hidden')) {
    const actionsRect=actions.getBoundingClientRect();
